{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_014FNUVaqZCzdNh8L7AMCE1P","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user wants me to generate detailed predicted experimental results for each \"planned\" experiment in the experiment_plan, under the \"median\" tier assumptions. I need to provide result_rationale for each prediction explaining why this result would occur under median tier conditions.\n\nLet me go through each planned experiment and generate predictions based on the median tier definition:\n\nMedian tier key characteristics:\n- Episode-level val success: 30-44%\n- Step-independent val success at convergence: 0-5%\n- Multi-seed std: 4-7pp\n- Sign vs outcome correlation: 0.80-0.95\n- Sign vs local quality correlation: 0.05-0.20\n\n\n- h-sweep cliff threshold: h=2-5\n- GAE vs episode-level delta: 5-15pp\n- Selective verification rate reduction: 20-40%\n- Selective success delta: 3-8pp\n- Action-change partial correlation: 0.10-0.20\n- Train action_is_valid: 0.60-0.75\n\nThe narrative is shifting toward positioning this as a diagnostic study that reveals why step-independent RL fundamentally struggles with multi-turn LLM agents, rather than focusing on dual contributions. Now I'm working through the first planned experiment to generate its predicted results. Looking at the remaining experiments, I need to flesh out the specifics for the 7B scaling work and the per-task breakdown analysis to understand how performance varies across different problem domains.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":20477,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":20477},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5d38cf08-9b48-449e-b610-0e2b32e2